---
---
<section class="across-ecosystem-section">
  <div class="container ecosystem-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Ecosystem</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Across the OPC UA ecosystem</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ecosystem-content">
      <p class="body-p">
        Downloads have grown more than 20&times; since 2020 &mdash; from a few
        thousand a month to over 500,000 &mdash; and have grown every year
        since the project's first stable release. After 12 years of
        continuous development, node-opcua has become the
        production-grade OPC UA implementation for the Node.js,
        JavaScript, and TypeScript ecosystem.
      </p>

      <p class="body-p">
        It sits alongside the mature implementations the OPC UA
        community maintains in other languages:
      </p>

      <ul class="peer-list">
        <li class="peer-item">
          <span class="peer-lang">C / C++</span>
          <span class="peer-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <a href="https://www.open62541.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="peer-link">open62541</a>
        </li>
        <li class="peer-item">
          <span class="peer-lang">Java</span>
          <span class="peer-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/eclipse-milo/milo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="peer-link">Eclipse Milo</a>
        </li>
        <li class="peer-item">
          <span class="peer-lang">.NET / C#</span>
          <span class="peer-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/OPCFoundation/UA-.NETStandard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="peer-link">OPC Foundation UA-.NETStandard</a>
        </li>
        <li class="peer-item">
          <span class="peer-lang">Python</span>
          <span class="peer-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/FreeOpcUa/opcua-asyncio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="peer-link">asyncua</a>
        </li>
        <li class="peer-item">
          <span class="peer-lang">Rust</span>
          <span class="peer-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/locka99/opcua" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="peer-link">rust-opcua</a>
          <span class="peer-note">(community project)</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="body-p">
        For the application and integration layer of industrial systems
        &mdash; gateways, MES, IIoT bridges, cloud connectors &mdash; Node.js and
        TypeScript bring typed APIs, async-first concurrency, full LSP
        tooling, and the npm ecosystem. Built on V8 and libuv, the async
        event loop fits OPC UA's subscription and notification model
        naturally &mdash; many concurrent sessions per process, no thread
        management. That is where node-opcua earns its place.
      </p>

      <p class="body-p">
        Sterfive participates in the OPC Foundation alongside the
        maintainers of these projects.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .across-ecosystem-section {
    padding: 6rem 0;
    background-color: var(--bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }
  .ecosystem-container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .section-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .section-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .ecosystem-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .body-p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .peer-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .peer-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .peer-lang {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
    min-width: 6.5rem;
  }
  .peer-arrow {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .peer-link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .peer-link:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .peer-note {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
